WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:18.282
Perda was startled by the certainty in Zira's eyes as she accused her and Zann of being from

2
00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:19.003
another world.

3
00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:21.224
"How do you know there are other worlds?"

4
00:00:21.725 --> 00:00:22.605
Zann blurted out.

5
00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:24.186
Zira smiled.

6
00:00:24.206 --> 00:00:25.887
"So it's true?"

7
00:00:25.907 --> 00:00:28.489
"Other worlds?"

8
00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:30.130
Vilkor let out a snort.

9
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.652
"What a ridiculous idea!"

10
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:34.944
Zira kept smiling.

11
00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:43.147
"It explains everything: their magic abilities, the flying chupo And the way you kids defeated the gorzog was

12
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:44.287
quite impressive.

13
00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:45.707
How did you do it?"

14
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:48.828
Perda still didn't trust Zira.

15
00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:52.429
She shot Zann a glance, hoping to stop him from answering.

16
00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:53.910
But he didn't notice.

17
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:56.670
"First, Perda used a Shield spell," he began.

18
00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.671
"Then she used a Shackle spell."

19
00:00:59.211 --> 00:01:01.752
He quickly explained how both spells were done.

20
00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.169
Zira asked several questions.

21
00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:10.132
Zann gave her more basic magic tips about friction, focusing words, and directing the mind.

22
00:01:10.152 --> 00:01:14.675
"I wish Zann would stop talking," Perda thought.

23
00:01:15.536 --> 00:01:16.996
But now it was too late.

24
00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:20.118
She tried to tell herself she was worried for nothing.

25
00:01:20.879 --> 00:01:24.901
After all, soon everyone in Terrica would be able to do magic anyway.

26
00:01:24.921 --> 00:01:27.762
"I see," Zira said at last.

27
00:01:27.782 --> 00:01:30.284
"Perhaps I'll try it myself."

28
00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:33.831
She rubbed her hands together, glancing around the area.

29
00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:37.093
Her eyes landed on the well, and she smiled.

30
00:01:37.113 --> 00:01:39.395
"Protect," she murmured.

31
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:45.841
Suddenly a tall stone wall appeared, completely surrounding the well.

32
00:01:47.282 --> 00:01:51.605
The only thing Perda could see was the top of the tree sticking out over the wall.

33
00:01:52.306 --> 00:01:56.309
Well, that and the magic energy still seeping out in all directions.

34
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.714
Now instead of drifting along the ground, it slid over the wall and dissipated.

35
00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.557
"Very impressive!"

36
00:02:05.097 --> 00:02:05.758
Vilkor said.

37
00:02:05.778 --> 00:02:08.560
"But now how am I supposed to reach my well?"

38
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.423
"The water is dangerous, my friend," Zira said.

39
00:02:12.443 --> 00:02:19.229
"Remember? This will keep our fellow villagers safe until we figure out how to purify it."

40
00:02:19.249 --> 00:02:27.176
"Wow, Zira is learning fast," Perda whispered to Zann and Mellis, feeling a little unnerved.

41
00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:31.767
"How did she figure out how to do such a large spell so quickly?"

42
00:02:31.787 --> 00:02:36.731
"She is known to be very wise," Mellis whispered back.

43
00:02:36.751 --> 00:02:39.253
"She must be," Zann murmured.

44
00:02:39.273 --> 00:02:43.157
"She's the only one in Terrica who believes other worlds exist."

45
00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.519
"She doesn't just believe it," Perda said.

46
00:02:46.539 --> 00:02:51.484
"We never mentioned being from another world to anyone here except Mellis.

47
00:02:52.324 --> 00:02:56.448
Zira must have known about other worlds even before we arrived!"

48
00:02:57.904 --> 00:03:01.126
Zing, who was still flying overhead, whistled loudly.

49
00:03:01.926 --> 00:03:04.228
A moment later Vilkor let out a shout.

50
00:03:04.248 --> 00:03:07.770
"Gorzogs!" He pointed toward the horizon.

51
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.531
"A whole herd of them is headed this way!"

52
00:03:10.551 --> 00:03:14.053
"Let's get out of here!"

53
00:03:14.433 --> 00:03:16.274
Zann said, whistling for Zing.

54
00:03:16.294 --> 00:03:18.095
"Wait." Perda said.

55
00:03:18.756 --> 00:03:24.039
The shackled gorzog still struggled against the magical restraints, drooling and snarling.

56
00:03:24.059 --> 00:03:26.240
"We can't leave it here like this."

57
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.401
Vilkor shrugged.

58
00:03:28.421 --> 00:03:29.441
"Why not?

59
00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:33.564
When the other gorzogs arrive, they'll see that it's helpless and devour it.

60
00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:36.686
That will decrease the local population by one."

61
00:03:37.427 --> 00:03:39.428
He obviously considered that a good thing.

62
00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:42.570
Perda hesitated, wondering if he was right.

63
00:03:43.391 --> 00:03:45.592
But Mellis pulled her hand out of her uncle's.

64
00:03:45.612 --> 00:03:47.794
"No!" she cried.

65
00:03:47.814 --> 00:03:49.955
"A gorzog can't help its nature.

66
00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.957
It would be cruel to leave it to be torn apart."

67
00:03:53.718 --> 00:03:56.820
She came closer, flinching when the gorzog growled at her.

68
00:03:57.728 --> 00:04:00.910
"Unshackle," she said, rubbing her hands together.

69
00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:07.333
The gorzog's shackles remained intact, though sparks bounced off them, exploding in the air.

70
00:04:07.854 --> 00:04:10.855
Mellis ducked, and the gorzog whined fearfully.

71
00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:14.457
"You can't remove someone else's Shackle spell," Zann said.

72
00:04:14.477 --> 00:04:17.159
"Only the person who created it can undo it."

73
00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:19.000
Perda stepped forward.

74
00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.461
"And that is me."

75
00:04:21.241 --> 00:04:22.402
She looked back at the others.

76
00:04:22.422 --> 00:04:26.284
"Get ready to zap away as soon as I release the gorzog."

77
00:04:29.224 --> 00:04:32.587
She unshackled the gorzog, and then everyone held hands.

78
00:04:32.607 --> 00:04:34.888
"Zap!" Zira shouted.

79
00:04:35.729 --> 00:04:36.950
They landed in a village.

80
00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:41.393
The street was narrow and unpaved and lined with shabby huts.

81
00:04:42.093 --> 00:04:44.895
However, the magic energy had clearly arrived.

82
00:04:45.576 --> 00:04:50.920
Green grass and bright flowers sprouted everywhere, and colorful fruit hung from the trees.

83
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:56.944
A bush covered in vibrant purple berries was visible over the walled yard of the nearest hut.

84
00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.822
"I wish Darb were here to identify those berries," Perda thought.

85
00:05:01.842 --> 00:05:06.083
"I feel as if I've seen them before, but I can't remember where."

86
00:05:06.103 --> 00:05:09.385
"Oh!" Vilkor looked around.

87
00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:11.866
"You've brought us to your home, Zira.

88
00:05:12.526 --> 00:05:14.687
I thought we were heading to my house."

89
00:05:14.707 --> 00:05:17.308
"I thought so too," Zann said.

90
00:05:17.328 --> 00:05:20.109
"I was about to zap us there, but Zira was faster."

91
00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.991
Perda nodded, surprised once again.

92
00:05:23.791 --> 00:05:29.399
Zapping was pretty basic magic, but it took time to learn how to land in a specific spot.

93
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.262
Zira had done it on her first try!

94
00:05:33.082 --> 00:05:34.704
Zira had a sly smile.

95
00:05:34.724 --> 00:05:37.226
"Let's step inside, Vilkor.

96
00:05:38.147 --> 00:05:39.948
We have much to discuss."

97
00:05:41.489 --> 00:05:43.551
The two adults disappeared into the hut.

98
00:05:43.571 --> 00:05:46.774
"I guess we're not part of the discussion," Zann said.

99
00:05:46.794 --> 00:05:49.496
"Let's zap back to the well and try to open the wormhole."

100
00:05:50.217 --> 00:05:51.418
"We can't go now."

101
00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:53.460
Mellis looked nervous.

102
00:05:54.156 --> 00:05:56.517
"Those gorzogs will still be sniffing around."

103
00:05:56.537 --> 00:05:59.558
"They can't climb that wall, can they?"

104
00:05:59.898 --> 00:06:00.558
Perda asked.

105
00:06:00.578 --> 00:06:02.938
"We could zap ourselves inside it."

106
00:06:03.659 --> 00:06:09.140
She grinned at Zann, remembering all the times he'd carelessly landed in a puddle or pond.

107
00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.821
"Zann is good at zapping into water."

108
00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:15.602
Just then several people raced into view on the street.

109
00:06:15.622 --> 00:06:18.063
"What's happening?"

110
00:06:18.603 --> 00:06:19.843
cried a wild-eyed woman.

111
00:06:20.603 --> 00:06:22.424
A tall man tore at his hair.

112
00:06:22.976 --> 00:06:24.737
"The whole world is changing!"

113
00:06:25.138 --> 00:06:25.618
he wailed.

114
00:06:25.638 --> 00:06:27.439
"It's the end of time!"

115
00:06:27.459 --> 00:06:29.420
"Where's the council?"

116
00:06:30.221 --> 00:06:32.342
A stout man shoved past the others.

117
00:06:32.362 --> 00:06:35.084
"We need to know what they plan to do about all of this!"

118
00:06:36.445 --> 00:06:38.566
Vilkor and Zira came back outside.

119
00:06:38.586 --> 00:06:40.788
"Calm down, everyone!"

120
00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:41.889
Vilkor cried.

121
00:06:41.909 --> 00:06:46.652
"There's no need to panic," Zira added loudly.

122
00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.053
"Everything is under control.

123
00:06:49.694 --> 00:06:52.796
Go home, and I'll update you as needed."

124
00:06:53.632 --> 00:06:55.774
She noticed the three kids and Zing.

125
00:06:55.794 --> 00:06:58.117
"That goes for you too.

126
00:06:58.777 --> 00:07:01.200
Return to Vilkor's house and stay there."
